sequenceDiagram
    participant Menu as menu:MainMenu
    participant G as game:Game
    participant R as repository:JsonGameRepository
    participant F as File system
    participant C as catalog:GameCatalog
    participant Factory as factory:IGameFactory
    participant H as history:CommandHistory
    participant Cmd as command:IMoveCommand

    Note over Menu,Cmd: SAVE during an interactive game
    Note over G: TakeHumanTurn parses save path; HandleControl invokes repository
    G->>R: Save(game, path)
    R->>G: ToSaveData()
    G->>H: Records()
    H-->>G: applied MoveRecords, oldest first
    Note over G: Board.ToSnapshot() and copied player inventories
    G-->>R: GameSaveData(version, keys, mode, level, board, inventory, moves)
    R->>F: WriteAllText(temporary, JSON)
    R->>F: Move(temporary, destination, overwrite=true)
    R-->>G: save succeeded
    Note over G: GameIO prints saved message; turn does not change

    Note over Menu,Cmd: LOAD from menu or after GameOutcome.LoadRequested
    Menu->>R: Load(path, catalog)
    R->>F: ReadAllText(path)
    F-->>R: JSON
    R->>R: RequireFields / Deserialize / ValidateData
    R->>C: Resolve(familyKey, variantKey)
    C-->>R: registered factory
    R->>Factory: CreateGame(GameSetup(mode, level))
    Note over Factory,G: Build parts, Assemble fresh game, attach view; Reversi sets centre disks
    Factory-->>R: fresh game
    R->>G: View.AutoRedraw = false
    loop each applied MoveRecord
        R->>R: reject record if previous Result.IsOver
        R->>G: Replay([record])
        G->>G: verify actor / Validate / CreateCommand
        G->>H: Do(command, State)
        H->>Cmd: Execute(State)
        Note over Cmd: ReversiPlaceCommand records CellChanges and calls Board.Apply
        Cmd-->>H: placement and flips applied
        Note over H: push undo, clear redo, increment MoveCount
        H-->>G: applied
        G->>G: OnMoveApplied / Win.Evaluate / TurnChanged
        G-->>R: replayed
    end
    Note over R,G: Empty history: Replay(empty) evaluates initial result
    R->>G: read Board.ToSnapshot() and player inventories
    G-->>R: reconstructed values
    R->>R: compare snapshots and inventories
    R->>G: restore AutoRedraw; Repository = this
    R-->>Menu: verified game with rebuilt undo stack
    alt loaded result is already complete
        Note over Menu,G: Menu renders the board and result; returns without another move
    else game is still in progress
        Menu->>G: Play(io)
    end
    Note over Menu,G: Failure branch: TryLoad catches error and keeps the current game
